From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:45:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs101: add the Mali-G78 GPU

The gs101 Mali-G78 MP20 as postmarketOS's gs101-mainline tree describes
it: a Valhall JM node at 0x1c500000 with its job, MMU and GPU
interrupts. There is no CMU_G3D driver yet, so it runs on the clock the
bootloader leaves running; the clocks property is a placeholder until
that driver exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
index bfceea548..8f57c2d74 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
@@ -1907,6 +1907,21 @@ sysreg_dpu: syscon@1c020000 {
 			clocks = <&cmu_dpu CLK_GOUT_DPU_SYSREG_DPU_PCLK>;
 		};
 
+		gpu: gpu@1c500000 {
+			compatible = "google,gs101-mali", "arm,mali-valhall-jm";
+			reg = <0x1c500000 0x5000>;
+			/*
+			 * TODO: placeholder until a CMU_G3D driver exists. ABL
+			 * leaves the G3D clock running; this is not that clock.
+			 */
+			clocks = <&ext_24_5m>;
+			interrupt-names = "job", "mmu", "gpu";
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 420 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 421 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 419 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		cmu_top: clock-controller@1e080000 {
 			compatible = "google,gs101-cmu-top";
 			reg = <0x1e080000 0x10000>;
